climate change is an unprecedented  global problem the emerging carbon  finance market with a potential for  enormous profits will play a critical  role in helping to solve this problem in  a major advance toward understanding  this new sector the Center for business  and the environment at Yale has  published carbon finance environmental  market solutions to climate change Brian  Garcia Brad gentry and Eric Roberts  developed and edited this important  report Brad Gentry director of the  Center for Business and the environment  at Yale well I think in terms of the way  I think about carbon finance it really  includes two concepts one of them is we  have the problem of climate change  because there's been no price on carbon  anybody burning coal anybody burning oil  anybody burning jet fuel or gasoline has  been putting carbon into the atmosphere  and not paying any price for it so one  part of carbon finance is monetizing the  cost of carbon to the extent that it's  causing pollution damage how do we  assign a price to that and one way to do  that is by limiting the amount of  emissions by putting a cap on the  emissions so if you put a cap on  emissions than different people who are  using fuels and many people need to  continue to use fuels we'll have to do  something to reduce them sometimes you  can buy more efficient engines sometimes  you can drive less whatever and then one  of the ways you can meet your cap is in  essence to pay other people to reduce  their emissions and take credit for the  reductions in their emissions that  wouldn't have happened before and if  you're going to for example pay somebody  else to build a wind farm pay someone  else to capture methane from farms pay  someone else to destroy industrial gases  from their plant you need to have a  system of financing those projects with  financing the construction of the wind  turbines the construction of the  digesters the construction of the  and so you bring those two concepts  together into carbon finance you're  putting a price on carbon you're  creating a commodity that's tradable and  you're creating a system that needs  finance in order to create the offsets  that can help people meet their  regulatory obligations to reduce their  emissions government carbon restrictions  and binding international agreements are  necessary components to a functioning  carbon market there's definitely a role  for government in creating carbon  markets we know that through science  that climate change is a human induced  phenomenon in that we have to achieve  certain reductions of the emissions of  greenhouse gases and to the extent  government can establish the goal and  the targets based on science of where we  need to be it effectively through  regulation will establish targets that  we have to achieve now once those  targets are achieved and they're set in  law then it's up to the market to figure  out ways of achieving those targets now  there's always an ongoing role for  government to monitor and make sure that  the market is operating correctly as it  was intended as it was structured  there's always a role for government to  make sure that the projects that  investors are investing in receiving  carbon value from are in fact delivering  the results that we expect of them  they're actually leading to a reduction  of greenhouse gas emissions so there's  always an ongoing role for gov for  government in the carbon markets  cap-and-trade has become the industrial  world standard tool for addressing  global warming the government puts a cap  on greenhouse gas emissions and issues  permits to companies for the right to  release carbon dioxide so cap-and-trade  system is a system established by  government with the intent of reducing  the level of greenhouse gas emissions  over time now that cap is established  with a base year and the government  wants to achieve over a number of years  a certain reduction reduction of co2  emissions to achieve a goal what  typically happens is here in the  Northeast we have the Regional  Greenhouse Gas Initiative that  established a cap-and-trade market the  first market of its kind here in the US  in fact several weeks back weeks ago the  first trades in the market occurred and  we have a price on carbon of three  dollars now effectively what that means  is if I'm a company that falls  underneath this cap and I am emitting  above what I should be emitting that I'm  now going to have to pay a price for  those emissions and it happens to be  three dollars per metric ton of co2 now  if I'm a company operating underneath  that value then I have the ability to  sell back into the system and earn some  revenue so cap-and-trade system is a a  government instituted standard or a  requirement for the market to achieve a  certain reduction of greenhouse gas  emissions cap and trade systems don't  exist without government the best role  for government in a cap-and-trade system  is setting a cap enforcing the cap and  reducing the cap over time so that you  actually get the incentives to reduce  more completely over time it then is  important for the government to make  sure that there are there's information  available around the market for the  allowances and the market for the  trading that takes place across  facilities under the cap and for helping  to ensure that there are sufficient  market structures so that the costs of  trading are not too high the joint  degree program offered by the Yale  School of Forestry and environmental  studies and the yale school of  management is preparing students to  become leaders of the new low carbon  economy I think now is the great time to  be at the Yale School of Forestry and  environmental studies the school is over  a hundred years old so it has this  tremendous legacy of trying to  understand and apply scientific  management principles to the planet to  forest systems in particular but lots of  other things we have had a joint degree  program with the school of management  for over 27 years where students have  come in and said we see an intersection  between business techniques business  resources and trying to solve  environmental problems and we want to  explore those under Rick Levin the  president of  Yale University in the last several  years we've seen a renaissance at Yale  in thinking about how to be a  sustainable institution not only reduce  our emissions of greenhouse gases but  also how to have more sustainable  sourcing of food how to have more  sustainable uses of water and things  like that and that creates just a  tremendous laboratory for learning on  campus so you have students not only  studying from textbooks but having  students engaging with helping make Yale  a more sustainable place and having  students engage with the network that  Yale has externally not only of alums  but of leaders and we're all about  solving the problems that matter how do  we get students and faculty engaged in  understanding the underlying issues the  pressing environmental issues in  preparing environmental leaders to then  go out into society and help us to solve  the problems that matter so we've  actually had a long-standing history of  a joint business environment degree  program here at Yale the Center for  business in the environment is a part of  the new vision of accelerating Yale's  role in preparing business leaders to  solve environmental problems to obtain a  copy of carbon finance environmental  market solutions to climate change visit  yale edu slash CBE y / carbon finance  2008 for more information about the Yale  School of Forestry and environmental  studies visit environment yale edu  you
 

